#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
xr — a friendly CLI/TUI wrapper around Xray-core for Arch Linux.

Single file, stdlib only. Manages saved servers (vless/vmess/trojan/ss),
subscriptions, a systemd --user service, system proxy, and latency tests.

Run `xr` with no args for the interactive Claude-Code-style shell, or use
subcommands: `xr add <link>`, `xr start`, `xr status`, `xr test`, ...
"""
